Can you not move it?

256
00:19:40,618 --> 00:19:42,161
What about your back?

257
00:19:42,244 --> 00:19:44,413
[screaming]

258
00:19:44,497 --> 00:19:48,083
-It hurts.
-Doctor.

259
00:19:48,167 --> 00:19:49,835
We found these meds on the desk.

260
00:19:56,050 --> 00:19:59,136
DEPARTMENT: SURGERY
ATTENDING PHYSICIAN: HA JEONGSOO

261
00:20:09,438 --> 00:20:10,439
Run her info.

262
00:20:11,106 --> 00:20:14,235
See if she's gotten a scan
at this hospital before.

263
00:20:15,569 --> 00:20:17,029
[typing]

264
00:20:17,112 --> 00:20:18,781
PATIENT INFORMATION
NAME: KIM GYEONGAE

265
00:20:18,864 --> 00:20:20,825
[doctor] Yes, we've got her MRI
from six months ago.

266
00:20:21,951 --> 00:20:24,036
Why would this woman,
who was your patient…

267
00:20:26,038 --> 00:20:27,957
kidnap my wife?

268
00:20:30,793 --> 00:20:34,171
The Dr. Ha I know
would never do anything like this.

269
00:20:37,591 --> 00:20:38,592
Who is it?

270
00:20:41,178 --> 00:20:42,888
Who's calling the shots?

271
00:20:44,306 --> 00:20:45,933
[stammering]

272
00:20:48,602 --> 00:20:50,479
Is it Director Ko Dongchan?

273
00:20:51,689 --> 00:20:53,315
[Dr. Ko] How are you going
to do this surgery?

274
00:20:54,108 --> 00:20:55,776
I'm going to do it by the book.

275
00:20:58,028 --> 00:20:59,113
"By the book"?

276
00:21:00,698 --> 00:21:03,325
Sure, you should, as a doctor.

277
00:21:04,785 --> 00:21:10,666
But not all life is of equal value.

278
00:21:12,585 --> 00:21:14,503
That woman is not a patient.

279
00:21:15,004 --> 00:21:17,298
She put your wife in danger

280
00:21:18,799 --> 00:21:20,885
and tried to take her life.

281
00:21:21,385 --> 00:21:22,428
RESTRICTED ACCESS

282
00:21:25,180 --> 00:21:27,516
[Dr. Ko] The OR is a strange place.

283
00:21:28,726 --> 00:21:30,936
Even if you prepare
for every possible scenario,

284
00:21:32,271 --> 00:21:34,648
you still run into unexpected situations.

285
00:21:36,734 --> 00:21:38,736
[Taeju] The immediate crisis is over,

286
00:21:39,528 --> 00:21:41,196
and her vitals are steady for now.

287
00:21:41,989 --> 00:21:42,990
[Dr. Ko] Good job.

288
00:21:43,073 --> 00:21:44,742
Well done,
STYLE
::cue()

289
00:21:46,410 --> 00:21:47,411
saving that woman.

290
00:21:51,665 --> 00:21:53,500
Dr. Ha. A moment.

291
00:22:02,134 --> 00:22:03,135
It's him, right?

292
00:22:06,221 --> 00:22:07,389
Dr. Ko,

293
00:22:08,140 --> 00:22:09,516
you,

294
00:22:10,184 --> 00:22:11,268
and this woman.

295
00:22:13,187 --> 00:22:14,605
What is the connection there?

296
00:22:15,105 --> 00:22:17,858
[scoffs, stammers]
How am I supposed to know?

297
00:22:19,026 --> 00:22:20,945
Why did you try to kill this woman?

298
00:22:21,695 --> 00:22:22,780
I don't know.

299
00:22:24,198 --> 00:22:25,658
I honestly don't know anything.

300
00:22:27,242 --> 00:22:28,243
Tell me.

301
00:22:29,745 --> 00:22:30,746
I know you know.

302
00:22:31,497 --> 00:22:32,498
I don't know, man.

303
00:22:33,499 --> 00:22:35,125
I was only doing what I was told.

304
00:22:36,293 --> 00:22:37,670
[nurse 2] Oh my! What…

305
00:22:41,215 --> 00:22:43,342
[objects clatter on floor]

306
00:22:46,720 --> 00:22:49,515
Dr. Kang, what are you doing here?

307
00:22:50,057 --> 00:22:52,726
I'm here to check on the patient
I operated on. Are you okay?

308
00:22:53,686 --> 00:22:54,728
Yeah.

309
00:22:56,563 --> 00:22:58,273
I was just about to leave.

310
00:22:58,941 --> 00:23:00,442
Can you wake him up?

311
00:23:02,069 --> 00:23:04,154
[sighs] Okay.

312
00:23:05,447 --> 00:23:08,283
Isn't it so tense
at the hospital these days?

313
00:23:08,826 --> 00:23:09,827
Is it?

314
00:23:10,494 --> 00:23:14,164
Well, nobody talks about it,
but everyone thinks it's weird.

315
00:23:14,248 --> 00:23:17,751
They're only keeping it quiet
because it's about Ms. Ko and Dr. Kang--

316
00:23:17,835 --> 00:23:19,169
[shouts, exclaims]

317
00:23:21,255 --> 00:23:23,215
[exclaims] Geez.

318
00:23:24,633 --> 00:23:25,968
That was Dr. Ha, wasn't it?

319
00:23:26,635 --> 00:23:27,886
What's wrong with him?

320
00:23:28,929 --> 00:23:30,514
-Darn it.
-Beats me.

321
00:23:44,069 --> 00:23:47,614
KO DONGCHAN, DIRECTOR

322
00:24:35,454 --> 00:24:36,455
[music ends]

323
00:24:38,874 --> 00:24:40,167
[Seyun's mother] Scary, isn't it?

324
00:24:42,044 --> 00:24:43,212
Mom.

325
00:24:43,837 --> 00:24:46,548
We took him in as part
of our family, and now this.

326
00:24:58,811 --> 00:25:00,646
How could he do something like that?

327
00:25:05,192 --> 00:25:06,235
How are you feeling?

328
00:25:07,945 --> 00:25:10,197
Maybe you should go back to the hospital.

329
00:25:11,323 --> 00:25:12,491
I'm fine, Mom.

330
00:25:13,325 --> 00:25:14,618
I just want to rest at home.

331
00:25:15,410 --> 00:25:16,411
Okay.

332
00:25:18,705 --> 00:25:20,415
We should get that fixed soon.
STYLE
::cue()

333
00:25:33,595 --> 00:25:36,056
SEOKGI CHUEOTANG

334
00:25:40,561 --> 00:25:43,105
Mom, I'll finish up here.

335
00:25:44,356 --> 00:25:45,566
You should head home.

336
00:25:50,946 --> 00:25:52,072
[sighs]

337
00:25:53,448 --> 00:25:54,741
[door opens]

338
00:25:54,825 --> 00:25:55,826
Sorry, we're…

339
00:26:06,670 --> 00:26:08,630
[gasps] Taeju.

340
00:26:10,340 --> 00:26:11,341
Hi, Mom.

341
00:26:12,885 --> 00:26:13,886
[shakily] Where…

342
00:26:13,969 --> 00:26:15,971
[♪ sentimental music playing]

343
00:26:18,682 --> 00:26:19,683
I'm sorry.

344
00:26:20,767 --> 00:26:22,227
Save your apology for later.

345
00:26:26,023 --> 00:26:27,191
It's fine.

346
00:26:28,692 --> 00:26:31,153
As long as you're okay.

347
00:26:33,614 --> 00:26:34,948
It's fine.

348
00:26:35,032 --> 00:26:37,576
Man, you look rough.

349
00:26:39,620 --> 00:26:41,622
-Are you okay?
-Yeah, I'm fine.

350
00:26:42,289 --> 00:26:45,959
What about Seyun? Is she okay too?

351
00:26:46,043 --> 00:26:48,378
Yeah, she's fine. She's safe.

352
00:26:49,129 --> 00:26:51,757
Oh, thank goodness.

353
00:26:53,091 --> 00:26:56,470
[crying] I'm so relieved.

354
00:26:57,429 --> 00:26:59,306
[sighing]

355
00:27:00,933 --> 00:27:02,100
I see.

356
00:27:04,353 --> 00:27:08,232
And so, have you talked to Seyun?

357
00:27:09,858 --> 00:27:12,653
Well, we haven't really had a chance
to talk things through yet.

358
00:27:12,736 --> 00:27:14,154
Why not?

359
00:27:15,405 --> 00:27:16,865
It's just… [chuckles]

360
00:27:17,532 --> 00:27:19,284
I don't want any more misunderstandings.

361
00:27:19,368 --> 00:27:21,495
Surely, it can't get any worse.

362
00:27:22,037 --> 00:27:24,456
You even shot up her parents' house,

363
00:27:24,539 --> 00:27:25,832
-so how could it--
-Taeyeong.

364
00:27:27,292 --> 00:27:28,460
[sighs]

365
00:27:31,672 --> 00:27:33,715
How are you going to set things straight?

366
00:27:34,883 --> 00:27:36,510
Just sit down and talk to her.

367
00:27:37,886 --> 00:27:40,639
You can't avoid it forever.

368
00:27:42,391 --> 00:27:44,267
Not yet. Well…

369
00:27:45,394 --> 00:27:47,771
There are a few things
I need to verify first.

370
00:27:48,897 --> 00:27:51,692
I can't really clear the air
with Seyun until I do.

371
00:27:54,111 --> 00:27:55,278
Taeju.

372
00:27:57,739 --> 00:27:58,740
Yes?

373
00:28:00,450 --> 00:28:03,996
Look, I don't know the ins and outs
of your marriage,

374
00:28:05,497 --> 00:28:07,290
but don't drag this out.

375
00:28:08,542 --> 00:28:10,085
The longer you let this sit,

376
00:28:10,961 --> 00:28:14,297
the more difficult it will be
to set things straight.

377
00:28:16,967 --> 00:28:19,219
And at that point, it'll be too late.

378
00:28:20,053 --> 00:28:22,472
Whatever you're going to do,
don't take too long.

379
00:28:22,556 --> 00:28:23,557
You understand?

380
00:28:26,018 --> 00:28:27,185
Yeah.

381
00:28:38,321 --> 00:28:41,366
Why don't you stay the night?

382
00:28:42,826 --> 00:28:43,827
Okay.

383
00:28:51,418 --> 00:28:53,712
-Here.
-Oh, no, I'm good.

384
00:28:53,795 --> 00:28:55,005
Let me pour you one.

385
00:29:01,470 --> 00:29:02,637
[laughs]

386
00:29:04,306 --> 00:29:05,307
What's so funny?

387
00:29:07,642 --> 00:29:10,395
You're just so fickle, aren't you?

388
00:29:12,230 --> 00:29:13,231
What do you mean?

389
00:29:13,857 --> 00:29:18,945
I mean, at first,
you couldn't live without her,

390
00:29:19,029 --> 00:29:22,240
and then you couldn't stand
living with her.

391
00:29:22,324 --> 00:29:26,203
And now, you're putting
your life on the line to save the woman

392
00:29:26,286 --> 00:29:28,246
you couldn't stand living with.

393
00:29:28,330 --> 00:29:29,581
[laughs]

394
00:29:29,664 --> 00:29:31,416
That's pretty fickle, isn't it?
STYLE
::cue()

395
00:29:34,377 --> 00:29:36,880
Do you know why I wanted
to end things with Seyun?

396
00:29:40,342 --> 00:29:41,343
Why?

397
00:29:45,514 --> 00:29:51,061
I didn't want her to be lonely
or in pain anymore.

398
00:29:56,149 --> 00:29:58,693
Why are you getting all deep on me now?

399
00:29:58,777 --> 00:30:00,153
Make it make sense.

400
00:30:01,738 --> 00:30:04,407
I thought it was the right thing to do.

401
00:30:05,075 --> 00:30:07,452
To let her off the leash.

402
00:30:12,874 --> 00:30:14,709
But I think I was wrong.

403
00:30:16,002 --> 00:30:17,629
I'm done running away now.

404
00:30:20,590 --> 00:30:23,593
Usually, these types of crimes
are committed by a lone wolf,

405
00:30:23,677 --> 00:30:25,971
but in this case,
we're looking at a married couple.

406
00:30:26,054 --> 00:30:27,514
MARRIED COUPLE IN ON THE CRIME

407
00:30:27,597 --> 00:30:29,057
Isn't that utterly shocking?

408
00:30:29,141 --> 00:30:30,809
It's beyond disturbing.

409
00:30:30,892 --> 00:30:32,561
And what's even more shocking?

410
00:30:32,644 --> 00:30:34,146
They barely even know me.

411
00:30:34,938 --> 00:30:36,606
They've never even talked to me,

412
00:30:36,690 --> 00:30:38,567
but the second
something like this happens,

413
00:30:38,650 --> 00:30:41,486
they all start running their mouths
like they know all about me.

414
00:30:41,570 --> 00:30:43,196
[TV host 1]
…that he was always kind and polite.

415
00:30:43,280 --> 00:30:46,199
And yet, he's accused
of committing these heinous acts.

416
00:30:46,783 --> 00:30:51,496
He was a kind teacher by day
but a depraved criminal by night.

417
00:30:51,997 --> 00:30:53,999
He was living an absolute double life.

418
00:30:55,083 --> 00:30:57,419
[TV host 2] Exactly.
That's what makes it so terrifying.

419
00:30:57,502 --> 00:30:58,503
Don't you think so?

420
00:30:58,587 --> 00:31:01,089
He didn't fit the profile of a criminal.

421
00:31:01,173 --> 00:31:03,925
No sinister looks, no red flags.

422
00:31:10,557 --> 00:31:15,478
JANG BONE-BROTH SUNDAEGUK

423
00:31:16,271 --> 00:31:19,274
-Hello.
-[owner] Hi, how are you? [chuckles]

424
00:31:22,694 --> 00:31:23,695
Oh, dear.

425
00:31:24,946 --> 00:31:26,198
[chuckles]

426
00:31:26,865 --> 00:31:29,534
You're back again. [laughs]

427
00:31:30,160 --> 00:31:31,328
-Enjoy.
-Thank you.

428
00:31:32,746 --> 00:31:34,414
Oh, hey. You're here.

429
00:31:34,497 --> 00:31:36,416
[chuckles] I wanted to grab a bite
before heading home.

430
00:31:36,499 --> 00:31:38,084
Well, I'm glad you came.

431
00:31:38,168 --> 00:31:41,046
Oh, right. Ever since you fixed it,

432
00:31:41,755 --> 00:31:44,591
that machine hasn't acted up once.
It's all thanks to you.

433
00:31:44,674 --> 00:31:46,801
[chuckling] Oh, come on, it was nothing.

434
00:31:47,510 --> 00:31:48,803
So, one gukbap?

435
00:31:49,387 --> 00:31:52,390
-Yeah.
-Okay, give me a moment. [laughing]

436
00:31:59,856 --> 00:32:01,483
[sighs]

437
00:32:03,360 --> 00:32:05,153
-[Dosik] Detective Oh!
-Yes, sir.

438
00:32:06,655 --> 00:32:10,116
FORENSICS

439
00:32:28,760 --> 00:32:29,886
Darn.

440
00:32:29,970 --> 00:32:31,513
[♪ ominous music playing]

441
00:32:41,606 --> 00:32:42,941
What the hell is this?

442
00:32:43,024 --> 00:32:46,361
[Hyeonsu]
Wow, this guy is completely nuts.

443
00:32:48,113 --> 00:32:50,115
[sighs]

444
00:33:01,543 --> 00:33:04,504
Collect every luminol-positive bloodstain
in the basement,

445
00:33:04,587 --> 00:33:05,755
and send them to the NFS.

446
00:33:06,256 --> 00:33:08,258
Request blood analysis
and DNA comparison too.

447
00:33:08,341 --> 00:33:09,342
Yes, sir.

448
00:33:10,343 --> 00:33:12,971
We don't know what else we'll find,
so search every inch.

449
00:33:13,054 --> 00:33:14,055
Yes, sir.

450
00:33:21,479 --> 00:33:22,522
What's that?

451
00:33:22,605 --> 00:33:23,606
It's a cell phone.

452
00:33:24,607 --> 00:33:26,026
It was under the fridge.

453
00:33:26,109 --> 00:33:27,569
-The fridge?
-Yeah.
STYLE
::cue()

454
00:33:30,447 --> 00:33:32,699
SEOKGI CHUEOTANG

455
00:33:32,782 --> 00:33:34,868
CLOSED FOR TODAY

456
00:33:52,344 --> 00:33:54,095
Dr. Ha. A moment.

457
00:33:58,475 --> 00:33:59,476
Dr. Kang!

458
00:33:59,559 --> 00:34:02,520
You didn't have to
come down here yourself, sir.

459
00:34:03,855 --> 00:34:07,275
I heard Dr. Kang personally verified
the label on the Park Dohyeon case today.

460
00:34:07,942 --> 00:34:11,571
The entire future of this hospital
is riding on this project.

461
00:34:13,782 --> 00:34:14,783
What about the logs?

462
00:34:14,866 --> 00:34:16,993
I've already backdated
the culture logs to match.

463
00:34:17,077 --> 00:34:18,620
What's going on here?

464
00:34:20,455 --> 00:34:21,539
Dr. Kang.

465
00:34:25,627 --> 00:34:27,253
[Taeju] What am I looking at?

466
00:34:29,172 --> 00:34:31,966
Why are there two stem cell samples
from the same patient?

467
00:34:33,176 --> 00:34:34,177
Dr. Ha.

468
00:35:19,681 --> 00:35:20,932
Take a sip.

469
00:35:25,437 --> 00:35:26,771
What's going on?

470
00:35:30,567 --> 00:35:31,818
[sighs]

471
00:35:34,362 --> 00:35:36,322
I wish you hadn't found out.

472
00:35:38,783 --> 00:35:43,037
Although I did think
that you would find out someday.

473
00:35:44,539 --> 00:35:47,709
Switching out a patient's
stem cell sample with a fetus's?

474
00:35:50,128 --> 00:35:51,212
Why would you do this?

475
00:35:52,088 --> 00:35:54,924
There are limits
to stem cells from an adult.

476
00:35:55,592 --> 00:35:57,343
You may be good,

477
00:35:58,261 --> 00:36:01,473
but you were far beneath
the success rate we're aiming for.

478
00:36:03,141 --> 00:36:05,518
However, after we switched them out,

479
00:36:06,311 --> 00:36:07,896
it was a different story.

480
00:36:08,938 --> 00:36:11,566
You did the surgeries, so you should know
STYLE
::cue()

481
00:36:12,275 --> 00:36:14,027
what we've accomplished.

482
00:36:14,819 --> 00:36:18,740
The patients consented to the procedure
thinking it was their own stem cells.

483
00:36:19,491 --> 00:36:21,367
This is completely illegal, Father.

484
00:36:21,451 --> 00:36:23,286
Those illegal procedures

485
00:36:24,245 --> 00:36:27,415
helped people regain movement
and stand on their own two feet.

486
00:36:28,666 --> 00:36:31,711
What do you make of those results?

487
00:36:35,048 --> 00:36:36,132
You've seen them.

488
00:36:36,800 --> 00:36:40,220
The faces they make after the procedure.

489
00:36:42,138 --> 00:36:43,848
Those people had given up,

490
00:36:44,891 --> 00:36:47,685
but now, they're hopeful
and excited about the future.

491
00:36:49,437 --> 00:36:50,438
Couldn't you just

492
00:36:50,939 --> 00:36:54,901
let them have that hope?

493
00:36:57,821 --> 00:36:59,364
That is not hope.

494
00:37:02,367 --> 00:37:06,162
Any hope that's built on a lie
is bound to fall apart.

495
00:37:08,331 --> 00:37:10,667
Knowingly giving them false hope…

496
00:37:13,086 --> 00:37:15,004
That's not hope. It's deception.

497
00:37:18,132 --> 00:37:20,301
Please count me out of this project.

498
00:37:27,058 --> 00:37:28,184
What about Seyun?

499
00:37:32,605 --> 00:37:34,524
What will you do about her?

500
00:37:44,033 --> 00:37:45,577
[steady beeping]

501
00:37:51,124 --> 00:37:54,627
[door opens, closes]

502
00:38:10,101 --> 00:38:11,394
[sighs]

503
00:38:22,363 --> 00:38:25,366
Can you check
Ms. Kim Gyeongae's vitals every hour?

504
00:38:25,450 --> 00:38:26,576
Okay, I will.

505
00:38:26,659 --> 00:38:28,077
But Dr. Choi.

506
00:38:28,912 --> 00:38:31,122
How long will she be at our hospital?

507
00:38:32,081 --> 00:38:33,082
Why?

508
00:38:33,625 --> 00:38:36,878
I mean, it's just uncomfortable.

509
00:38:36,961 --> 00:38:38,421
Everyone feels that way.

510
00:38:38,504 --> 00:38:40,715
Well, she's still a patient.
She has to recover.

511
00:38:45,428 --> 00:38:48,056
I'm going to head home.
Let me know when she wakes up.

512
00:38:48,139 --> 00:38:49,349
Okay.
STYLE
::cue()

513
00:39:39,399 --> 00:39:40,858
[phone buzzing]

514
00:39:41,943 --> 00:39:44,028
INCOMING CALL
GRANDDAUGHTER

515
00:39:44,112 --> 00:39:46,114
[buzzing continues]

516
00:39:50,451 --> 00:39:53,079
Grandma! Why can't I reach you?

517
00:39:58,126 --> 00:39:59,335
Who are you?

518
00:40:00,169 --> 00:40:01,504
Catch your breath now.

519
00:40:02,088 --> 00:40:03,089
Have a seat.

520
00:40:08,511 --> 00:40:09,929
Don't you remember me?

521
00:40:12,098 --> 00:40:14,559
Sweetheart, can you set his table?

522
00:40:14,642 --> 00:40:15,643
Okay, Grandma.

523
00:40:17,937 --> 00:40:19,772
Your grandmother's told me all about you.

524
00:40:20,523 --> 00:40:22,442
-Nice to meet you.
-Likewise.

525
00:40:23,026 --> 00:40:24,777
You know Woori Together Medical Center?

526
00:40:25,486 --> 00:40:27,613
She works as a nurse there.

527
00:40:27,697 --> 00:40:29,157
Ah!

528
00:40:29,741 --> 00:40:30,825
Yeah, I've been there.

529
00:40:31,743 --> 00:40:34,787
She helps me out
whenever she can, after her shift.

530
00:40:34,871 --> 00:40:37,874
She's not like
the other young people these days.

531
00:40:37,957 --> 00:40:40,418
That's amazing. You must be proud of her.

532
00:40:41,169 --> 00:40:43,379
What are you doing here?
[breathing heavily]

533
00:40:44,756 --> 00:40:46,340
Where's my grandma?

534
00:40:47,300 --> 00:40:48,384
Your grandma?

535
00:40:48,968 --> 00:40:50,386
She's gone on a trip.

536
00:40:50,970 --> 00:40:53,723
She was in a hurry,
so she wanted me to watch the place.

537
00:40:54,223 --> 00:40:55,933
But that's her phone.

538
00:40:57,268 --> 00:40:59,937
Oh, yeah. She must've forgotten.

539
00:41:03,691 --> 00:41:04,942
Where is my grandma?

540
00:41:07,361 --> 00:41:09,238
I said, she's on a trip.

541
00:41:09,322 --> 00:41:12,116
Why would she suddenly go on a trip
without even telling me?

542
00:41:12,200 --> 00:41:14,744
Guess she didn't feel like telling you.

543
00:41:15,912 --> 00:41:17,080
Where's my grandma?

544
00:41:17,580 --> 00:41:19,248
Where is she?

545
00:41:19,332 --> 00:41:21,751
I'm going to call the cops.

546
00:41:21,834 --> 00:41:23,586
If you do, I feel like I might…

547
00:41:26,339 --> 00:41:27,882
forget where your grandma is.

548
00:41:30,051 --> 00:41:31,052
My grandma…

549
00:41:32,553 --> 00:41:34,055
Is she safe?

550
00:41:38,810 --> 00:41:40,103
We'll see.

551
00:41:43,898 --> 00:41:45,316
It depends on how you do.

552
00:41:51,531 --> 00:41:53,074
[Taeju] Anyway, that being said…

553
00:41:54,117 --> 00:41:55,993
I want you to get rid of my wife.

554
00:41:56,077 --> 00:41:57,995
[Manhui] What? What did you say?

555
00:41:58,663 --> 00:42:00,081
[Taeju] Get rid of my wife.

556
00:42:01,332 --> 00:42:02,333
Ms. Ko.

557
00:42:04,460 --> 00:42:06,129
How does that make you feel?

558
00:42:07,547 --> 00:42:08,714
I know this is fake.

559
00:42:10,174 --> 00:42:12,301
There's no way he said anything like that.

560
00:42:12,885 --> 00:42:14,595
I know you don't want to believe it.

561
00:42:15,096 --> 00:42:16,347
But hey.

562
00:42:16,430 --> 00:42:22,353
You already know
that your husband doesn't love you.

563
00:42:33,614 --> 00:42:34,699
No!

564
00:42:37,493 --> 00:42:40,913
That video. It's all a misunderstanding.

565
00:42:40,997 --> 00:42:42,540
I can explain all of it.

566
00:42:42,623 --> 00:42:44,292
I'm telling you the truth.

567
00:42:44,959 --> 00:42:47,461
Please. Please just believe me.

568
00:42:48,129 --> 00:42:49,881
Seyun.

569
00:42:49,964 --> 00:42:51,465
Seyun, come on.

570
00:42:51,549 --> 00:42:54,218
Seyun. Come on. Please.

571
00:42:54,302 --> 00:42:55,428
Seyun.

572
00:42:55,511 --> 00:42:57,263
Seyun, can you hear me?

573
00:42:57,346 --> 00:42:58,931
Hey, are you okay?

574
00:43:09,317 --> 00:43:10,735
[Dr. Ko] What did you say?

575
00:43:11,485 --> 00:43:12,486
What?

576
00:43:13,446 --> 00:43:15,198
What are you saying?

577
00:43:15,698 --> 00:43:17,450
Ugh. Calm down.

578
00:43:17,533 --> 00:43:19,243
I can't understand a word!

579
00:43:20,703 --> 00:43:21,704
What?

580
00:43:22,496 --> 00:43:24,290
Kang Taeju was there?

581
00:43:25,082 --> 00:43:26,584
Why are you telling me this now?

582
00:43:27,126 --> 00:43:29,253
You know what a huge problem
you've caused?
STYLE
::cue()

583
00:43:29,337 --> 00:43:30,880
Where are you right now?

584
00:43:30,963 --> 00:43:33,799
I'll take care of it myself.
Just come to the hospital.

585
00:43:34,717 --> 00:43:36,302
No.

586
00:43:36,385 --> 00:43:39,472
Just come back to the hospital!
[clicks tongue]

587
00:44:13,714 --> 00:44:15,174
Taeju?

588
00:44:27,895 --> 00:44:29,897
[♪ ballad playing]

589
00:44:29,981 --> 00:44:31,232
[Dr. Ko] What about Seyun?

590
00:44:31,941 --> 00:44:33,442
What will you do about her?

591
00:44:34,235 --> 00:44:36,696
What if the whole world finds out?

592
00:44:37,905 --> 00:44:39,323
A father who's a criminal,

593
00:44:40,241 --> 00:44:44,412
the hospital that turned a blind eye,
and the husband at the center of it all.

594
00:44:45,705 --> 00:44:49,417
Seyun will have to shoulder all of that.

595
00:44:49,917 --> 00:44:53,754
Whether you do the surgery or not,
that's your call.

596
00:44:55,381 --> 00:44:59,802
But it won't be you who pays the price.

597
00:45:00,845 --> 00:45:02,346
It will be Seyun.

598
00:45:05,099 --> 00:45:09,103
What her life will be like after that…

599
00:45:11,397 --> 00:45:12,982
Have you thought about that?

600
00:45:14,942 --> 00:45:16,944
[♪ song continues]

601
00:46:04,825 --> 00:46:05,826
[song ends]

602
00:46:15,961 --> 00:46:17,838
I'm here to check on her.

603
00:46:18,589 --> 00:46:19,590
[officer] Okay.

604
00:46:23,844 --> 00:46:25,846
[medical equipment beeping]

605
00:47:04,385 --> 00:47:05,386
It's me.

606
00:47:06,887 --> 00:47:09,890
Her BP and heart rate seem normal,
and her breathing's stable.

607
00:47:11,016 --> 00:47:14,270
She's not conscious yet,
but she seems stable.

608
00:47:15,104 --> 00:47:16,272
[sighs]

609
00:47:17,231 --> 00:47:18,524
Keep an eye on her.

610
00:47:19,024 --> 00:47:20,025
Okay.

611
00:47:20,526 --> 00:47:22,987
Oh, and one more thing.

612
00:47:24,405 --> 00:47:27,408
Dr. Kang stopped by her room yesterday.

613
00:47:28,242 --> 00:47:29,577
What are you…

614
00:47:30,953 --> 00:47:32,788
I thought he was arrested.

615
00:47:32,872 --> 00:47:34,707
I'm not sure what happened either.

616
00:47:35,249 --> 00:47:37,418
I talked to another nurse,

617
00:47:38,252 --> 00:47:41,881
and it seems he snuck in
while the police officer was asleep.

618
00:47:45,926 --> 00:47:47,178
Tell me all the details.

619
00:47:48,262 --> 00:47:50,848
Apparently, he said he came
to check on the patient

620
00:47:52,057 --> 00:47:53,684
and then just left.
STYLE
::cue()

621
00:48:10,201 --> 00:48:12,536
NEUROSURGERY
HA JEONGSOO

622
00:48:12,620 --> 00:48:16,165
[breathing heavily]

623
00:48:16,248 --> 00:48:18,542
INCOMING CALL
ILSEUNG CAPITAL

624
00:48:18,626 --> 00:48:21,128
[phone buzzing]

625
00:48:29,970 --> 00:48:32,014
CAPTAIN, MAJOR CRIMES UNIT 1
LIEUT. JANG DOSIK

626
00:48:33,015 --> 00:48:34,058
Captain.

627
00:48:34,141 --> 00:48:35,142
Yeah?

628
00:48:35,643 --> 00:48:36,727
You should see this.

629
00:48:36,810 --> 00:48:39,104
COME TO THE HOSPITAL
WE NEED TO TALK

630
00:48:39,188 --> 00:48:40,189
"To the hospital?"

631
00:48:40,856 --> 00:48:43,317
-Is that all?
-Yeah, everything else was wiped clean.

632
00:48:44,902 --> 00:48:47,530
[sighs] Get Kim Gyeongae's phone
to Forensics now.

633
00:48:47,613 --> 00:48:49,907
-We have to recover all of it.
-On it, sir.

634
00:48:54,745 --> 00:48:57,581
She's been in touch
with someone in the hospital.

635
00:49:00,668 --> 00:49:02,419
[tires screech]

636
00:49:04,922 --> 00:49:06,840
[phone buzzes]

637
00:49:08,634 --> 00:49:12,137
ILSEUNG CAPITAL: PAY BACK BY MORNING,
OR WE'LL SEE YOU AT YOUR GIRL'S PRESCHOOL

638
00:49:13,806 --> 00:49:15,057
[sighs]

639
00:49:15,891 --> 00:49:17,393
Darn, Kang Taeju.

640
00:49:18,435 --> 00:49:20,271
If only he hadn't shown up.

641
00:49:30,948 --> 00:49:31,949
Dr. Ha!

642
00:49:33,909 --> 00:49:34,910
Oh, hi.

643
00:49:41,125 --> 00:49:42,710
Working late tonight, Dr. Ha?

644
00:49:44,169 --> 00:49:45,170
Uh, yeah.

645
00:49:45,796 --> 00:49:46,797
Me too.

646
00:49:49,508 --> 00:49:51,260
[tires screech]

647
00:50:05,441 --> 00:50:06,692
[car alarm beeps]

648
00:50:20,581 --> 00:50:22,833
[sighs] Dr. Ha!

649
00:50:25,961 --> 00:50:27,171
How did this happen?

650
00:50:28,213 --> 00:50:29,632
I told you to be cautious!

651
00:50:30,174 --> 00:50:31,508
Dr. Ko?

652
00:50:32,134 --> 00:50:34,136
[♪ tense music playing]

653
00:50:35,679 --> 00:50:36,680
[stammers]

654
00:50:38,766 --> 00:50:40,309
What the hell are you doing here?

655
00:50:41,727 --> 00:50:45,230
I could ask you the same thing.
What are you doing here so late?

656
00:50:46,440 --> 00:50:48,192
Oh, let me guess.

657
00:50:50,027 --> 00:50:53,614
You're not here to see Dr. Ha, are you?

658
00:50:54,281 --> 00:50:56,700
I'm the one asking questions.

659
00:50:58,035 --> 00:50:59,536
What are you doing here?

660
00:51:00,120 --> 00:51:01,747
I just had to check something.

661
00:51:02,414 --> 00:51:03,749
"Check something"?

662
00:51:05,125 --> 00:51:08,045
Yeah, it turns out
that woman, Kim Gyeongae,

663
00:51:08,671 --> 00:51:10,506
was one of our patients.

664
00:51:11,799 --> 00:51:14,051
And Dr. Ha was her attending physician.

665
00:51:17,096 --> 00:51:18,597
Were you aware of that?

666
00:51:20,474 --> 00:51:21,642
[scoffs]

667
00:51:22,226 --> 00:51:23,227
So?

668
00:51:24,937 --> 00:51:26,105
What are you getting at?

669
00:51:26,897 --> 00:51:30,943
I caught him right before he injected
potassium chloride into her IV.

670
00:51:31,652 --> 00:51:33,278
I barely stopped him.

671
00:51:34,988 --> 00:51:36,281
What possible reason

672
00:51:37,408 --> 00:51:41,578
could he have
to do such a thing to that woman?

673
00:51:46,792 --> 00:51:49,378
That's what I wanted to know.

674
00:51:50,129 --> 00:51:55,634
But she's unconscious,
and I have no clue where Dr. Ha is.

675
00:51:56,385 --> 00:51:58,387
So I'm out of options.

676
00:52:00,305 --> 00:52:02,224
Considering you're the hospital director,

677
00:52:03,475 --> 00:52:05,561
I thought you might know a thing or two.
STYLE
::cue()

678
00:52:13,736 --> 00:52:15,571
One of our patients…

679
00:52:16,280 --> 00:52:17,823
Dr. Ha's patient

680
00:52:19,408 --> 00:52:21,285
was one of Seyun's kidnappers.

681
00:52:22,911 --> 00:52:24,496
Why on earth did she do that?

682
00:52:28,500 --> 00:52:31,336
You should ask that
to that criminal of a woman.

683
00:52:33,088 --> 00:52:35,174
Why are you asking me?

684
00:52:36,633 --> 00:52:39,803
Sure, but don't you think
it's a bit weird?

685
00:52:40,721 --> 00:52:42,055
That woman

686
00:52:43,557 --> 00:52:46,727
seems to know so much about you.

687
00:52:47,603 --> 00:52:49,605
[♪ tense music playing]

688
00:52:51,356 --> 00:52:53,901
You've known Kim Gyeongae
all along, haven't you?

689
00:52:54,651 --> 00:52:57,529
After what you did to my wife…

690
00:52:58,989 --> 00:53:01,241
Maybe you're not worth saving.

691
00:53:07,331 --> 00:53:11,585
I could say the same thing
about that father-in-law of yours.

692
00:53:12,294 --> 00:53:18,342
That scumbag extending his own lifespan
by using those unborn babies.

693
00:53:20,844 --> 00:53:24,848
She knew that you were using
stem cells from fetuses.

694
00:53:25,808 --> 00:53:27,684
She knew all the details.

695
00:53:32,981 --> 00:53:35,359
Isn't that why you tried to shut her up…

696
00:53:37,653 --> 00:53:39,363
with the help of Dr. Ha?

697
00:53:40,781 --> 00:53:42,491
Why did you try to kill this woman?

698
00:53:42,574 --> 00:53:44,284
I don't know.

699
00:53:45,202 --> 00:53:46,829
I honestly don't know anything.

700
00:53:47,621 --> 00:53:48,872
I know you know.

701
00:53:48,956 --> 00:53:50,165
I don't know, man.

702
00:53:50,999 --> 00:53:53,502
I was only doing as I was told. Okay?

703
00:53:55,337 --> 00:53:57,256
You and Kim Gyeongae.

704
00:53:59,550 --> 00:54:01,260
What is the connection between you two?

705
00:54:04,805 --> 00:54:07,057
The woman who knows the secret
behind the project

706
00:54:08,308 --> 00:54:10,185
kidnapped my wife.

707
00:54:11,103 --> 00:54:12,729
Is that really a coincidence?

708
00:54:13,438 --> 00:54:14,690
So what?

709
00:54:16,942 --> 00:54:18,485
Are you suggesting

710
00:54:19,778 --> 00:54:22,322
that I had my own daughter kidnapped?

711
00:54:23,448 --> 00:54:24,575
Did you not?

712
00:54:25,450 --> 00:54:26,785
You've lost your mind.

713
00:54:28,745 --> 00:54:29,788
Well…

714
00:54:30,998 --> 00:54:32,499
Do you have any evidence?

715
00:54:35,168 --> 00:54:36,461
You don't, do you?

716
00:54:38,589 --> 00:54:40,340
If you want to know so badly,

717
00:54:42,551 --> 00:54:45,637
ask that woman once she wakes up.

718
00:54:47,264 --> 00:54:48,473
Either that

719
00:54:50,017 --> 00:54:53,186
or ask Ha Jeongsoo,
wherever the hell he is.

720
00:55:09,328 --> 00:55:10,329
[music ends]

721
00:55:28,305 --> 00:55:29,765
CALLING
NS_HA JEONGSOO

722
00:55:30,724 --> 00:55:32,726
[line ringing]

723
00:55:32,809 --> 00:55:34,436
[sighs]

724
00:55:34,519 --> 00:55:37,022
[ringing continues]

725
00:55:51,286 --> 00:55:52,496
[ringing stops]

726
00:55:53,080 --> 00:55:55,082
PARKING

727
00:55:56,375 --> 00:55:58,377
[♪ tense music playing]

728
00:56:09,304 --> 00:56:10,514
WING B, B3F
STYLE
::cue()

729
00:56:40,293 --> 00:56:42,295
[line ringing]

730
00:56:45,424 --> 00:56:47,592
[phone ringing in distance]

731
00:57:01,481 --> 00:57:03,984
[distant ringing continues]

732
00:57:28,091 --> 00:57:30,302
[ringing continues]

733
00:57:47,360 --> 00:57:50,363
DIRECTOR KANG TAEJU

734
00:58:42,791 --> 00:58:47,629
THE HUSBAND

735
00:58:47,712 --> 00:58:50,173
[♪ closing theme song playing]

736
00:59:28,253 --> 00:59:30,755
[Taeju] I wanted to check the applications
and selection records…

737
00:59:31,631 --> 00:59:33,174
[Seyun] Is it related to my dad?

738
00:59:33,758 --> 00:59:36,428
[Hyeonsu] About the phone
that Ha Jeongsoo had on him…

739
00:59:36,511 --> 00:59:39,347
It's the same number
that contacted Kim Gyeongae.

740
00:59:39,431 --> 00:59:41,850
I'll stay on Ms. Kim Gyeongae's case.

741
00:59:41,933 --> 00:59:46,229
Both my husband and I
were just pawns in this game.

742
00:59:46,313 --> 00:59:49,983
[Taeju] If someone actually tried
to have you killed through Dr. Ha…

743
00:59:50,066 --> 00:59:52,277
Do you think that person
will leave you alone now?

744
00:59:52,819 --> 00:59:55,322
[granddaughter] If someone ever finds out,
I'll be in huge trouble.

745
00:59:55,405 --> 00:59:56,406
[Manhui] Today.

746
00:59:57,073 --> 00:59:58,408
It'll be over today.

747
00:59:59,743 --> 01:00:01,745
Translated by Hyun Sik Yoon

